    <!-- Help Modal (accessible dialog) -->
    <div id="help-modal" class="fixed inset-0 z-50 hidden" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/60" data-help-backdrop></div>
        <div role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="help-title" aria-describedby="help-desc" class="relative max-w-3xl w-full m-4 mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-gray-800 rounded-xl shadow-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 w-full relative border border-gray-700">
                <button id="close-help-modal" class="absolute top-4 right-4 text-gray-500 hover:text-white" aria-label="Close Help">&times;</button>
                <h2 id="help-title" class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Welcome to <span class="text-accent">Pixelogic</span></h2>
                <p id="help-desc" class="text-gray-400 mb-6">Quick overview. For a complete tab and sub-section manual, open the Help tab from the sidebar.</p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm leading-6">
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Pixel Designer</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Define the real-world size (m/ft/cm), panel size and resolution.</li>
                            <li>Calculated metrics show both reduced and decimal aspect ratios, for example 5:4 (1.25:1).</li>
                            <li>Choose a visual style (checker/gradient), border and numbering.</li>
                            <li>Enable/disable individual panels by clicking in the preview.</li>
                            <li>Duplicate pixel maps to try variations quickly.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Map Annotations</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Overlay info, markers (circle, cross, corners), and corner circles.</li>
                            <li>Include Metrics adds screen size, pixel size and both aspect-ratio formats to the centre badge.</li>
                            <li>Add a logo, color bars, and adjust shared color/thickness.</li>
                            <li>Coordinates overlay shows (X, Y) top-right with adjustable size.</li>
                            <li>Live preview with zoom/fitting; thumbnails for quick switching.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">2D Visualizer</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>View the selected Pixel Map at full pixel resolution.</li>
                            <li>Fit, zoom, and export the layout image if needed.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Output Canvas</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Compose multiple pixel maps into a single output canvas.</li>
                            <li>Multi-select maps with Ctrl/Shift, then drag as a group.</li>
                            <li>Delete selected maps (Delete/Backspace); undo/redo with Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y.</li>
                            <li>Crop by panels, draw annotations, and view fluorescent canvas bounds.</li>
                            <li>Export PNG/JPG; use the Transparent PNG toggle for alpha exports.</li>
                            <li>Scrollbars appear when the canvas is larger than the viewport.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">LED Patching</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Configure wall and tile specifications on the left, inspect the live patch diagram in the centre, and review processor, port, and circuit allocation on the right.</li>
                            <li>Use <strong>Auto Patch</strong> for Snake/ZigZag routing, or <strong>Draw Lines</strong> to build signal and power paths tile-by-tile.</li>
                            <li>In Draw Lines mode, click or drag through orthogonally adjacent tiles. A tile can belong to only one route of the active type.</li>
                            <li>Use <strong>Next Port</strong> to finish a data line and advance from C1-P1 onward; power drawing advances to the next circuit.</li>
                            <li>The dock beneath the wall shows active assignment, tile count, pixels or amps, live load percentage, and overload status.</li>
                            <li>Undo/Redo edits, Clear All to wipe the active manual layer, then Undo if the clear was accidental. Select Done to leave drawing mode.</li>
                            <li>Toggle Data and Power overlays, use FIT or zoom controls, then export PNG or the professional 2-page PDF report.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">PDF Export</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Render a spec sheet with title, details, delivery specs and preview.</li>
                            <li>Map auto-fitting controls let you position the preview precisely.</li>
                            <li>Fill the Title Block (project, venue, client, version).</li>
                            <li>Typography supports Windows system fonts (fallback to PDF core fonts).</li>
                            <li>Step sections are collapsible to reduce clutter.</li>
                            <li>File Delivery Spec: Edit opens the form; Save closes it.</li>
                            <li>Include Pixel Pitch in Details; auto-computes from panel size/res if missing.</li>
                            <li>Pixel-map details include total pixel size and aspect ratio in PDF and PPTX exports.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Power Calc</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>65 tile models across 10 brands with real bench-measured Amp values at 100% and 50% brightness.</li>
                            <li>Per-scenario breakdown: Full Red, Green, Blue, White and Standby — per tile, total and per phase.</li>
                            <li>1-Phase or 3-Phase mode with automatic tile distribution across L1/L2/L3.</li>
                            <li>Recommended breaker size calculated at 1.25× safety factor for each scenario.</li>
                            <li>Summary KPIs: total A, active power (kW), apparent power (kVA at PF 0.9), worst-case breaker per phase.</li>
                            <li>Export a professional dark-theme PDF report with summary KPIs, scenario breakdown, phase distribution and reference data tables.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Projects</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Manage projects (rename, delete, mark saved) and reopen later.</li>
                            <li>New and saved projects are shown side by side.</li>                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Circular LED</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Plan curved/circular LED screens with diameter/radius metrics.</li>
                            <li>Preview ring modules, circumference, and measurement helpers.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Misc Tools (Aspect Ratio + LTC)</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Aspect Ratio Calculator: preset and custom aspect calculations with visual reference.</li>
                            <li>LTC Generator: create SMPTE LTC WAV files with configurable frame rate, sample rate, and bit depth.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">3D Visualizer</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Interactive 3D textured model of every project map with orbit, pan, zoom and per-map transforms.</li>
                            <li>Each screen has a boxed label with map name, physical W × H and pixel resolution.</li>
                            <li>Add stage decks, select Move and drag a deck directly, or use Span to LED Bottom to align and match width.</li>
                            <li>Stage callouts clearly show deck name and W × D × H dimensions.</li>
                            <li>Toggle UV overlay, depth grid, X/Y/Z axes and extrude depth while editing.</li>
                            <li>Camera Views: save named camera angles, recall with one click, delete individually or Clear All.</li>
                            <li>Auto Revolve mode for hands-free presentations; adjustable spin speed.</li>
                            <li>Save PNG/JPG exports a clean full-resolution snapshot without editor axes or transform gizmos.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-accent">Projector Test Pattern</h3>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-200">
                            <li>Generate projector alignment patterns, including dome mode.</li>
                            <li>Adjust overlaps, hatching, grid, numbers, and unit settings.</li>
                            <li>Sub-tabs: Settings, Flat Calculator, Curved Calculator, Circular/Dome Calculator.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-6 border-t border-gray-700 pt-4 text-sm">
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-accent mb-2">Typical Workflow</h3>
                    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-200">
                        <li>Create or open a project in the Projects tab.</li>
                        <li>In Pixel Designer, set physical size, LED panel details, and style.</li>
                        <li>Refine overlays in Map Annotations.</li>
                        <li>Send to Output Canvas to compose multi-map layouts.</li>
                        <li>Plan signal distribution in LED Patching; generate CAD drawings & engineering sheets.</li>
                        <li>Calculate power requirements in Power Calc before site day.</li>
                        <li>Export PNGs or generate a PDF spec in PDF Export.</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-3">Tip: Use the duplicate buttons in Pixel Designer and Output Maps to iterate without losing your original.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Input Modal -->
    <div id="input-modal" class="fixed inset-0 bg-black/60 items-center justify-center z-50" style="display: none;">
        <div id="input-modal-content" class="bg-gray-800 rounded-xl shadow-2xl p-8 w-full max-w-md m-4 relative border border-gray-700">
